# The exact wording of the out-of-range f32 literal diagnostic — the binary32
# twin of tests/diag/float_lit_overflow.ty.
#
# The lexer's DBL_MAX test cannot catch this: 3.5e38 is an ordinary binary64 and
# only becomes an infinity where the f32 destination narrows it. Before this
# existed the program below compiled clean and printed `inf`.
#
# The same guard covers the other three routes a literal takes to f32 — a binop
# against an f32 operand, an [f32] element, and an f32 arg or return.
fn main():
    a: f32 = 3.5e38
    println(str(a))
